\f6\b0\fs52 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
volatile
\f4\fs50  is a 
\f2\b Java keyword
\f4\b0  used with 
\f2\b variables
\f4\b0 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls21\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
It tells the 
\f2\b JVM and CPU
\f4\b0  that the variable\'92s value 
\f2\b may be modified by multiple threads
\f4\b0 .\
\ls21\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Ensures that 
\f2\b reads/writes to that variable are directly done in main memory
\f4\b0 , not cached in CPU registers or thread-local caches.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 In simple words: 
\f6\fs52 volatile
\f4\fs50  guarantees 
\f2\b visibility
\f4\b0  of changes to variables across threads.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs62 \cf0 2. Key Points About 
\f3\fs65 volatile
\f2\fs62 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls22\ilvl0
\fs50 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
