\f1\b\fs84 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
Q13. How do you write a native SQL query in JPA?\
\
Ans \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs54 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
1. Using 
\f3\fs57 @Query
\f2\fs54  with 
\f3\fs57 nativeQuery = true
\f2\fs54 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs66 \cf0 When using 
\f2\b Spring Data JPA
\f4\b0 :\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs68 \cf0 \
public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> \{\
\
    @Query(\
        value = "SELECT * FROM users u WHERE u.email = :email",\
        nativeQuery = true\
    )\
    User findByEmail(@Param("email") String email);\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f8\fs66 \cf0 \uc0\u55357 \u56393 
\f4  Here:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls32\ilvl0
\f6\fs68 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
value
\f4\fs66  = the SQL query\
\ls32\ilvl0
\f6\fs68 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
nativeQuery = true
\f4\fs66  tells JPA it\'92s raw SQL, not JPQL\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs54 \cf0 2. Using 
\f3\fs57 @NamedNativeQuery
\f2\fs54  (on Entity)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs66 \cf0 You can define a named native query on your entity class:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs68 \cf0 \
@Entity\
@NamedNativeQuery(\
    name = "User.findByStatus",\
    query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE status = ?1",\
    resultClass = User.class\
)\
public class User \{\
    @Id\
    private Long id;\
    private String email;\
    private String status;\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs66 \cf0 Then call it like:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs68 \cf0 \
List<User> users = entityManager\
        .createNamedQuery("User.findByStatus", User.class)\
        .setParameter(1, "ACTIVE")\
        .getResultList();\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs66 \cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs54 \cf0 3. Using 
\f3\fs57 EntityManager.createNativeQuery()
\f2\fs54 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4\b0\fs66 \cf0 If you want more flexibility (manual use):\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs68 \cf0 \
List<Object[]> results = entityManager\
    .createNativeQuery("SELECT u.id, u.email FROM users u WHERE u.status = ?")\
    .setParameter(1, "ACTIVE")\
    .getResultList();\
\
for (Object[] row : results) \{\
    Long id = ((Number) row[0]).longValue();\
    String email = (String) row[1];\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

